      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T15:00:03Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): tool editor fields, clamping check and a side drawing to scale\n\nU10 of the tool library refit (#3663). The Tool tab reads as the mock-up:\nName, Type, Tool number; a CUTTER group with flutes, helix angle, tool\nmaterial and centre cutting; a SHANK group; then the assembly group with\nHolder, Stick-out, the holder's gauge length, the derived gauge length with\nits sum, an \"Open holder\" link and one clamping-range check line that names\nthe holder that refuses the shank. The side drawing is the default view:\nit draws the flute lines, the spindle nose outline and the holder's name,\nbuilt with the cached model, so a still frame builds nothing.\n\nFixes #4336\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
